 Default invocation checks native execution custody before requiring completed evidence. An `in_progress` attempt is pending only while the latest exact scan execution is running under a positively verified native PID/start fingerprint, its progress is newer than the native inactivity timeout, and elapsed run time is below the existing native live-owner stale bound. Both bounds must be finite and positive; unknown custody, stale progress, an old attempt, a failed/terminal execution or an unlimited policy cannot suppress failure. This pending outcome emits no notification and never writes or claims a fresh complete snapshot. Native cron owns the active scan timeout/failure delivery; this script does not add delays or schedules.
 
